WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.738 --> 00:00:04.405
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:10.496 --> 00:00:14.986
- When you find a tree
that has an apple in it

00:00:14.986 --> 00:00:18.415
and just discovering new varieties.

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:21.332
It's just, I mean, I live for that.

00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:31.447
I'm Andy Brennan.

00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:33.962
My wife and I, we around our town

00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:36.919
and we forage for wild apples

00:00:36.919 --> 00:00:40.589
and we make it into a series of ciders

00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:43.465
based on where the apples are located.

00:00:43.465 --> 00:00:45.318
- [Man] You sell
at the Gramercy Tavern?

00:00:45.318 --> 00:00:49.485
- Yeah, yeah Gramercy Tavern, um,
which I've only eaten at once.

00:00:50.529 --> 00:00:54.311
I know it's famous and
especially their wine menu

00:00:54.311 --> 00:00:56.006
is somewhat famous.

00:00:56.006 --> 00:00:59.340
- Having cider made
from wild-foraged fruit

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.852
is really unusual, something
that can only be done

00:01:01.852 --> 00:01:03.954
in very small amounts.

00:01:03.954 --> 00:01:07.871
What comes out of the
bottle is really special.

00:01:13.227 --> 00:01:15.571
- We go out into the woods.

00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:19.148
We go to places where apples
are not at all influenced

00:01:19.148 --> 00:01:20.898
by human cultivation.

00:01:23.301 --> 00:01:25.560
We're searching the woods
and sometimes it's difficult

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.670
to find the trees.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.800
And If the light doesn't hit the
silver in the trunk just right,

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.002
you may not even know it's an apple tree.

00:01:34.002 --> 00:01:36.879
You're in luck when you
find not just one or two,

00:01:36.879 --> 00:01:41.046
but a whole forest of trees
which sometimes does exist.

00:01:46.924 --> 00:01:49.346
What I love is discovering varieties

00:01:49.346 --> 00:01:51.488
that are just so peculiar.

00:01:51.488 --> 00:01:55.155
You would never find
'em in a grocery store.

00:01:56.792 --> 00:01:57.939
The other day we found an apple

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:00.616
that has red flesh, so you bite into it

00:02:00.616 --> 00:02:03.378
and it just looks like a pomegranate.

00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:06.547
They're telling us, "Process."

00:02:06.547 --> 00:02:08.727
It takes about four hours to grind

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:12.640
and press enough juice to fill a barrel.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.779
I think of those barrels as bears.

00:02:14.779 --> 00:02:16.465
It's hibernating.

00:02:16.465 --> 00:02:19.236
Nine months after you
collected the apples,

00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:21.153
that's when it's ready.

